@startuml
autonumber
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 10

box "Cloud & OEM Connected Backend" #LightYellow
participant "Mobile Companion App" as App
participant "Entitlement & SUMS Backend" as Backend
end box

box "Vehicle Edge Compute Platform" #LightCyan
participant "Telematics Gateway / SUMS" as OTA
participant "Feature Access Controller (Crypto MCU)" as Auth
participant "Vehicle Digital Cockpit (HMI)" as HMI
participant "Automated Driving Domain Controller" as AD
end box

== 1. Subscription Provisioning & Cryptographic Lease Push ==
App -> Backend: Purchase L3 Highway Chauffeur Subscription (Driver Profile: Alice)
Backend -> Backend: Generate RSA-4096 / ECDSA-P384 Signed Lease Token (Valid: 30 Days)\nBind RXSWIN type approval signature (UN R156)
Backend -> OTA: Encrypted HTTPS / TLS 1.3 Token Delivery
OTA -> Auth: Store Signed Lease Token into Non-Volatile Secure Element
Auth --> HMI: Feature Entitled: L3 Highway Chauffeur Ready

== 2. Drive Start & Offline Tunnel Grace Period Handling ==
Driver -> HMI: Ignition ON (Binds Driver Profile A via UWB Key)
Auth -> Auth: Verify Local Lease Signature & Validity Timestamp
alt Token Valid & Network In Coverage
    Auth -> AD: Authorize L3 Automated Driving Functionality
    HMI -> Driver: Display Ready: L3 Available (Teal Highway Icon)
else Cellular Dead Zone (e.g., Bavarian Mountain Tunnel)
    Auth -> Auth: Check Offline Elapsed Time (< 24 Hour Grace Window)
    Auth -> AD: Authorize L3 Cruise (Offline Lease Cache Active)
    HMI -> Driver: L3 Engaged (Offline Grace Indicator Active)
end

== 3. Critical Safety Edge Case: Mid-Drive Subscription Revocation ==
Backend -> OTA: Push Subscription Expiry / Revocation Flag (Payment Default)
OTA -> Auth: Transmit Revocation Command
Auth -> Auth: Check Current Dynamic Driving State
alt Vehicle State == L3_ACTIVE_CRUISING
    note over Auth, AD #Pink
        **CRITICAL AUTOMOTIVE SAFETY RULE (ISO 26262 / UN R157)**:
        Under no circumstances may automated driving be deactivated abruptly mid-drive!
        Enforce **Graceful Session Lock**:
        - Feature remains 100% active until driver manual disengagement or safe ODD exit.
        - Revocation is staged to prevent re-engagement on the next ignition cycle.
    end note
    Auth -> Auth: Set Flag: DISABLE_ON_NEXT_IGNITION_CYCLE
    Auth --> HMI: Maintain Active Driving Display (Silent Background Lock)
end
@enduml
